# Repository-root build context.
#
# Neither image is built from here — api/Dockerfile and client/Dockerfile each
# take their own directory as the context, and each has its own .dockerignore
# beside it. This file is the safety net for anyone who runs a build from the
# root anyway, and its first job is the same as theirs: keep the secrets out.
#
# A .env copied into a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and
# stays readable after a later layer deletes it.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.mcp.json

# --- Installed dependencies --------------------------------------------------
# Platform-specific and rebuilt inside the image. Copying the host's is how a
# Windows binary ends up in a Linux image.
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
api/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Caches and test artefacts -----------------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vitest/
coverage/
.paddleocr/
.paddlex/
ocr/models/
ocr/_smoke/

# --- History and documents ---------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
*.log
logs/

# --- Editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
